    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nThis bright and spacious three-bedroom, two-bathroom semi-detached home on Cabinteely Avenue offers an excellent opportunity to acquire a wonderful family property in one of South Dublin's most desirable locations. Well maintained and presented in good condition throughout, the accommodation is generous and versatile, with two reception rooms providing excellent living and entertaining space. To the rear is a great private garden, offering a peaceful and secure outdoor space for relaxing, entertaining and family life. The property also benefits from a garage, which offers exciting potential for conversion to suit the needs of the new owners.\n\nThe property is quietly positioned in a peaceful cul-de-sac, while being just a short walk from Cabinteely Village, where residents can enjoy a popular selection of restaurants, cafés and local amenities. There is also plenty of scope to extend the property, subject to the necessary planning permission, making this an ideal home for those looking to add space and value over time. The surrounding area is exceptionally well served by green space, with Cabinteely and Clonkeen Parks close by, providing wonderful opportunities for walks, outdoor activities and family days out.\n\nLocation is undoubtedly one of this home's greatest attractions. Excellent transport links provide easy access to Dublin City and surrounding areas, while Dun Laoghaire is just a short distance away. The property is also ideally positioned close to some of Dublin's best schools, making it particularly appealing to young families. Combining generous accommodation, a private garden, excellent potential and a superb location close to parks, village amenities, transport and schools, this is a fantastic opportunity to create a long-term family home in a highly sought-after part of South Dublin.\n\nProperty Highlights\n\n- Three-bedroom, two-bathroom semi-detached home\n- Bright and spacious accommodation\n- Two reception rooms\n- Great private rear garden\n- Garage with potential for conversion\n- Excellent potential to extend, subject to planning\n- Good condition throughout\n- Quiet cul-de-sac setting\n- Highly sought-after Cabinteely location\n- Short walk to Cabinteely Village, restaurants and cafés\n- Close to Cabinteely and Clonkeen Parks\n- Excellent transport links\n- Surrounded by attractive green spaces\n- Ideal location for young families\n- Short distance to Dun Laoghaire\n- Close to some of Dublin's best schools"
      },
